cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  This is a fork of Douglas Colkitt's integer-mult-bounds, used for a
  just-for-fun experiment with AI-generated math.
  Credit Douglas Colkitt's integer-mult-bounds baseline and the OpenAI paper
  listed in references. If referring to this experiment, include its Git commit.
title: "Integer multiplication, just for fun"
authors:
  - family-names: DePoint
    given-names: Owen
    alias: odepoint
    website: "https://github.com/odepoint"
license: Apache-2.0
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/odepoint/intmultspam"
url: "https://github.com/odepoint/intmultspam"
abstract: >-
  A fork of Douglas Colkitt's integer-mult-bounds, used by odepoint for a
  just-for-fun experiment to see how far AI can push an integer-multiplication
  bound. Includes generated notes, code, exact-arithmetic output, and source
  patches, building on the original repository and OpenAI's underlying paper.
  The math is largely unverified. This repository
  documents a hobby project, not a research paper; the included checks cover
  finite identities and arithmetic rather than the full mathematical argument.
keywords:
  - integer multiplication
  - computational complexity
  - exact arithmetic
  - parameter optimization
  - AI-generated math
references:
  - type: software
    title: "A sharper exponent for integer multiplication"
    authors:
      - family-names: Colkitt
        given-names: Douglas
    year: 2026
    repository-code: "https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds"
    url: "https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/tree/6e564879f51ae16f23d392e9e196c605f36d90df"
    commit: "6e564879f51ae16f23d392e9e196c605f36d90df"
    license: Apache-2.0
  - type: unpublished
    title: "Integer multiplication below n log n"
    authors:
